"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids, August to September and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years. In 2025 on the middle, January to February was 33% of normal and August to September was 48%, while June to July came in at 142%. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, and grid 24151 was at 47% that year.</p>"}
